WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.200
But… what else was left on the Moon?

00:03.200 --> 00:07.200
The astronauts didn’t only collect Moon rocks and take photographs.

00:07.200 --> 00:12.000
They also brought amazing objects that are still on the Moon today.

00:12.000 --> 00:17.000
A very special mirror called the Laser Ranging Retroreflector.

00:17.000 --> 00:20.200
It is used to measure the exact distance between Earth and the Moon.

00:20.200 --> 00:23.300
It needs no electricity—and it still works today!

00:23.300 --> 00:30.500
Thanks to it, we know the Moon moves about 3.8 centimeters away from Earth each year. Little by little!

00:30.500 --> 00:34.800
A moonquake detector called a seismometer.

00:34.800 --> 00:39.200
Did you know the Moon shakes too? Yes! There are moonquakes on the Moon!

00:39.200 --> 00:46.200
And that’s not all—the astronauts left a tiny disc with goodwill messages from 73 countries.

00:46.200 --> 00:51.400
And guess what? Peru also sent a message that traveled all the way to the Moon!
